      "independent_solution": "For the first graph, x is nonzero and xy=-5, so its branches lie in quadrants II and IV. The candidate points (-1,5), (1,-5), (-5,1), and (5,-1) each have product -5. For the second graph, xy=7.5 implies y=7.5/x and branches in I and III; (1,7.5), (3,2.5), (-1,-7.5), and (-3,-2.5) each have product 7.5. Both graphs have the coordinate axes as asymptotes and no axis points. Option 2 replaces the first constant by -1; option 3 replaces the second constant by 1. Exactly option 1 satisfies both equations.",
